# Python Port Plan — Step 03 · The Prompt Builder

## Purpose

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/03_prompt_builder` to Python, producing
`week1_baseline/python/03_prompt_builder` that is behaviourally equivalent:
same `PromptBuilder` shape (`to_messages`/`to_tools`/`to_api_payload`/
`headers`/`url`), same five backends (`Anthropic`, `Gemini`, `Ollama`,
`OllamaCloud`, `OpenAI`) with the same `MODELS` tables and cost/window
metadata, same `UnsupportedModelError`, same `example.rb` console output
(modulo the accepted language-level divergences already established in
`01_struct`/`02_the_registry` plus new ones called out below).

This is the fourth entry in the `docs/plans/python_port/<step>` series (see
[`context.md`](context.md) for the index). `02_the_registry` is done; this
step adds `PromptBuilder` and `Backends::{Base,Anthropic,Gemini,Ollama,
OllamaCloud,OpenAI}` on top of it. No HTTP calls happen anywhere in this
step — backends only serialize `Context` into the request payload shape
each API expects; nothing is POSTed.

`Registry`, `Tool`, `Message` are **unchanged** on the Ruby side (confirmed
with `diff` against `02_the_registry`'s copies — byte-identical) and get
copied forward again. `Context` is unchanged in behaviour (only a trailing
newline differs). `Config` gained a `PROMPTS_DIR` constant on the Ruby
side in this step — but the Python port already added `PROMPTS_DIR` back in
`02_the_registry`'s `config.py`, so **no change is needed there**; Python is
simply ahead of where Ruby was. `errors.rb` gains one new class,
`UnsupportedModelError`, alongside the existing `UnknownToolError`.

