**Known upstream quirk to preserve, not fix** (same category as prior
README-vs-code gaps): `PromptBuilder#to_messages` calls
`@backend.to_messages(@context.messages)` — a **single** argument. But
`Ollama`/`OllamaCloud`/`OpenAI`'s `to_messages` is defined as
`to_messages(system, messages)` — **two** required arguments (they need the
system prompt to prepend it as a `role: system` message). Calling
`builder.to_messages` directly would raise `ArgumentError` in Ruby for
those three backends; it only works for `Anthropic`/`Gemini`, whose
`to_messages` takes one argument. `example.rb` never actually calls
`builder.to_messages` directly (only `builder.to_api_payload`, which calls
each backend's own `to_messages` internally with the right arity), so this
never surfaces at runtime — but it's a real, reproducible inconsistency in
the public `PromptBuilder` API. Recommend porting it faithfully (same
arity mismatch, same `TypeError` on `builder.to_messages()` for those three
backends) and documenting it in the Python README's differences/quirks
section, rather than silently fixing it — fixing would be a behavioural
fork from the Ruby original this step is meant to mirror.

